==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|shěd}}, {{IPA|en|/ʃɛd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-shed.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛd|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*skey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|scheden}}, {{m|enm|schede}}, from {{inh|en|ang|scēadan}}, {{m|ang|scādan|t=to separate, divide, part, make a line of separation between; remove from association or companionship; distinguish, discriminate, decide, determine, appoint; shatter, shed; expound; decree; write down; differ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skaiþan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skaiþaną}} (compare {{cog|fy|skiede}}, {{cog|nl|-}} and {{cog|de|scheiden}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skeyt-|t=to cut, part, divide, separate}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*skey-}}.

See also {{cog|cy|chwydu|t=to break open}}, {{cog|lt|skėsti|t=to spread}}, {{m|lt|skíesti|t=to separate}}, {{cog|cu|цѣдити|t=to filter, strain}}, {{cog|grc|σχίζω|t=to split}}, {{cog|xcl|ցտեմ|t=to scratch}}, {{cog|sa|च्यति|tr=cyáti|t=he cuts off}}). Related to {{l|en|shoad}}, {{l|en|shit}}, {{l|en|sheath}}.

